s adds in a \"Use Local Space\" button to the 2D editor like the 3D editor currently has. By default, Godot uses local space in the 2D editor anyway, so the actual functionality of this PR comes from turning it off, which allows you to do global space transformations. For global translations, this works exactly as you'd expect. For global scale, I made it so that when you scale along the x-axis, it attempts to preserve the height of the object, and when you scale along the y-axis, it attempts to preserve the width of the object. I personally find it intuitive, but there might be a more obvious way that I'm missing, so I'd really appreciate feedback on this.\r\n\r\nKeep in mind that by default, \"Use Local Space\" is on, so there shouldn't be any immediate difference.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"ht